2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/bd/57/c9/a1/5344485ed8de8e42/freudenberg_alte_flecken_original.jpg?hash=fcb84a3b8e4d1cba89650d59e673d26d3cc0de91617072a3b87f82a52e127eff.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE The village of Freudenberg with the Evangelical church with it's tower, originally a castle tower built before1389 with a “Gefängnis” which is a jail or prison that served as a Hexenturm, witch's tower during the witch trials that
3 CONC  plagued the area for many years.  
3 CONT
3 CONT Anna Catharina Friesenhagen was baptised in this church on 31 May 1663, her parents, Jacob Friesenhagen and Anna Maria Dresler, were married in this church on 20 May 1651 and this church was attended by many of her ancestors.
3 CONT
3 CONT I took this picture from the park above the old section of Freudenberg, the Alter Flecken, complete with cobblestone streets and the half-timbered buildings all date from the 1600's.  This is our base in the Siegerland on the Germ
3 CONC anna Foundation Germany Trip.
3 CONT
3 CONT Barbara Price, Trustee/Genealogist
3 CONT The Germanna Foundation
