2 NOTE The title for this map states it's "of How the Germantown of 1717 may have looked," but this is the 1714 Colonists, not the 1717 Colonists.  The 1717 Colonists never lived at Germantown.  Also, the river labeled as the Rapidan is 
3 CONC actualy Licking Run, the Rapidan River is located further south at Germanna, not Germantown.  I'm posting a map of Germantown that was published by Dr. BC Holtzclaw and Prof. Woodford B. Hackley, both Germanna descendants, in Germ
3 CONC anna Record No. 2: Germantown Revisited first in 1962, reprinted in 1980 and 2005 by the Germanna Foundation.
3 CONT
3 CONT Holtzclaw and Hackley physically walked the entire Germantown plat using the original Germantown survey and deed to John Hoffman, Jacob Holtzclaw and John Fishback recorded on 22 Aug 1724 in Northern Neck Grant Book A, p. 63.  The
3 CONC y walked all the metes and bounds and also recorded the disposition of each family lot until it left the families.
3 CONT
3 CONT Source: Dr. BC Holtzclaw and Prof. Woodford B. Hackley, Germanna Record No. 2: Germantown Revisited, (Culpeper, Virginia: The Memorial Foundaion of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, Inc., 1962).
3 CONT
3 CONT Barbara Price, Trustee/Genealogist
3 CONT The Germanna Foundation
