1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georg_Christoph_Lichtenberg '''Georg Christoph Lichtenberg'''] was a German scientist, satirist, and Anglophile. As a scientist, he was the first to hold a professorship explicitly ded
2 CONC icated to experimental physics in Germany. Today, he is remembered for his posthumously published notebooks, which he himself called Sudelbücher, a description modeled on the English bookkeeping term "scrapbooks", and for his disc
2 CONC overy of the strange tree-like patterns now called Lichtenberg figures.
