1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Anna Catharine Fishback ''' 
2 CONT * Born	Abt 1714 	Germanna, Virginia 
2 CONT * Died	1775 	Rectortown, Fauquier County, Virginia 
2 CONT * Person ID	I081081 
2 CONT * Daughter of Johannes Fischbach,   b. 12 Jul 1691, Trupbach, Nassau-Siegen (now Westphalia, Germany),   d. Between 11 and 19 Mar 1733, at or near Germantown, Prince William (now Fauquier) County, Virginia and Agnes Catharina Häge
2 CONC r,   b. 26 Oct 1697, Siegen, Nassau-Siegen (Germany),   d. Abt 1725, Germantown, Prince William (now Fauquier) County, Virginia (Age 27 years) 
2 CONT * Married Johannes Richter,   b. 1 Dec 1711, Trupbach or Siegen, Nassau-Siegen (now Germany),   d. 11 Mar 1773, Rectortown, Fauquier County, Virginia (Age 61 years); they married Bef Mar 1733 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT #John Rector,   b. Abt 1734, Germantown, Prince William (now Fauquier) County, Virginia,   d. Bef 5 Nov 1772, Fauquier County, Virginia (Age ~ 38 years) 
2 CONT #Catherine Rector,   b. Abt 1735, Virginia Find all individuals with events at this location,   d. Abt 1790  (Age ~ 55 years)   
2 CONT #Henry Rector,   b. 1 Mar 1736,   d. Between 2 Apr and 26 Nov 1781, Fauquier County, Virginia 
2 CONT #Jacob Rector,   b. Abt 1740, Virginia,   d. 1781, Bedford County, Virginia  (Age ~ 41 years)   
2 CONT #Daniel Rector,   b. 8 Feb 1742,   d. 1 May 1814, Clark County, Ohio (Age 72 years)   
2 CONT #Charles Rector,   b. 24 Apr 1742, Fauquier County, Virginia,   d. 1833, Sevier County, Tennessee   (Age 90 years)   
2 CONT #Benjamin Rector,   b. Between 1744 and 1748,   d. Abt 1808  (Age ~ 64 years)  
2 CONT #Elizabeth Rector,   b. Abt 1746   
2 CONT #Frederick Rector,   b. 16 Jul 1750, Rectortown, Fauquier County, Virginia,   d. 24 Oct 1811, Oak Hill near Kaskaskia, Illinois Territory (now Illinois)  (Age 61 years)  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://germannafamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I081081&tree=tree1
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From  http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Anna_Fischbach_%285%29_
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes (John) Rector married Anna Chatherine Fischback born in 1714 at the Germanna Colony in the new colony...married her in 1732.Anna Catherine died abt 1775 (1789) at Rectortown, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes and Anna fischbach Rector had at least the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #John Rector b. 3/1/1734 at Rectortown, died 65/30/1773.  Married his first cousin Catherine Rector b. 1744  died 1818 possibly daughter of Henry Rector and nancy ann Spencer.  they had the following children  1) Mary Polly Rector
2 CONC  b. 1766 2)George Rector v. 1769 and died 1844.
2 CONT #Catherine Rector  b. 1735 at Germantown Va, and died also unknown date in Germantown Va.  married Thomas Glascock b. 1731-d. 1793. had three children. a). Elizabeth Glascock b. 1763-1837 b).Susan Glascock  b. 1765-1857 c). George
2 CONC  Glascock  b. 1767-1832.
2 CONT #Henry  Rector  b. 3/1/1735 Fauquier County, Va d. 11/26/1781 Rectortown, Va (Maidstowne va)  in 1765 Henry married Mary Glascock  b. 1734-1822 Fauquier Va they had 7 children. a). Frances Rector  1762-1799 b). Elizabeth Rector  1
2 CONC 766-1839 c). William jRector  1768-1834 d). Margaret Rector 1770-1833 e). Catherine Rector 1772-1862 f). John Alexander Rector  1774-1855 g). Enoch Rector  1776-1816
2 CONT #Charles Rector  b. 4/24/1742-1833 in Sevier Tennessee.  Was married twice.  First time to Elizabeth Charlotte Wharton married 1764.  She was born in 1742 and died in 1776.  They had the following children. a).  Benjamin Rector 17
2 CONC 65-1863 b). Landlel Rector  1767 c). William Rector 1768 d). Quilla Rector  1770  e). Charlotte Rector  1772-1840 f.  Hannah Rector  1774-1830 g). Cumberland Rector  1775 h).  Millie Rector  1776 second he was married to Elizabeth
2 CONC  Glascock after 1776.  She was born b. 1755.  jThey had the folloiwning children a). Morgan Rector  b.1778-1863 b). Celia Rector  b.1780 c).Charles Riggles Rector (?) d).Clara Rector  b1784-1801
2 CONT #Elizabeth Rector  b. 12/14/1743 at Rectortown, Va, died 1817 at Winchester Clark, Kentucky.  about 1760 she married Francis Hieronymus  1729-1814 in Va.  they had a). Susan Hieronymus  1764-1844 b). Ludwell Hieronymus  1768 c).  
2 CONC Benjamin Hieronymus  1773-1860 d).  Catherine Hieronymus  1774-1836 e). Pendleton Hieronymus  1775-1846 f). Henry  Hieronymus 1776-1831 g).  Nancy Hieronymus  1778 h). Francis Hieronymus  1783-1810 i).  Samuel R. Hieronymus  1786-
2 CONC 1855
2 CONT #Benjamin Rector  b 1/24/1744 germantown, Va.  died 4/2/1808  Rectortown, Va married Sarah Kerr  1748-1826  on 5/9/1769 in Fauquier County, Va. children follows a).  Ludwell Rector  1771 b).  Thomas Recotr  1774-1825 c).  Charles 
2 CONC Rector  1776-1859 d).  Sally Rector  1778 e). Molly Mary Rector  1780-1863 married her  lst cousin Enoch f). Nancy Rector 1783 g). Rebecca Rector 1785 h).Daniel Rector 1789
2 CONT #Jacob Rector  b. 1745 Fauquier Va died 1773 possibly b 1747  (10/5/1747-1779). married Jane Preston (?) b. 1742-1813 a). Charlotte Rector b1762 b). Lewis Rector b. 1765-1830 c). Martin Rector  b1768-1832 d).  Sally Rector b1770 e
2 CONC ).Elizabeth Rector  b1772 f). Rebecca Rector   b1777 g). John Josiah Rector  b1778-1856
2 CONT #Frederick Rector  b 7/16/1750 Rectortown, Va  died 9/18/1811 at Oak Hill Kankakee Illinois.  on 2/7/1770 he married Elizabeth Conner daughter of Lewis and Ann Wharton Conner in Fauquier Va.  children follow possibly more... a). N
2 CONC ancy Ann Rector  b1771-1815  her son THOMAS JAMES SEVIER CONWAY WAS THE 1ST GOVERNOR OF ARKANSAS. b). Lucy Rector b1772 c). Sally Rector  b.1773 d). Wharton Rector b. 1775-1826 e). Molly Rector  b1776 f). William Rector  b1778-182
2 CONC 7 g). Elias Rector  b1780-1822 note HIS ELDEST SON HENRY MASSEY RECTOR WAS ELECTED GOVERNOR OF ARKANSAS IN 1850. h). Elizabeth Rector  b 1781-1858 i).John Rector  b. 1783-1805 j).Nelson Rector b1784 k)  Thomas C. Rector b1786 l)  
2 CONC Stephen Rector b1788-1826 m).  Samuel Rector (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE;  GERMANNA COLONY OF VIRGINIA WEB SITE
2 CONT
2 CONT ALSO SEE RECTORTOWN VA. WEBSITE/GENEOLOGY/FAMILY SEARCH....
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From the "Find a Grave" website...
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna 'Catherina' died "after 03 January 1789". Wife of 'John' Johannes Rector. Daughter of Johannes 'John' Fischbach and Agnes Haeger Fischbach. Last name Fischbach to Fishback. Anna Catherina and her husband John Rector/Ritcher w
2 CONC ere cousins and were married about 1732. They had at least 10 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ++John Rector married prior to 11 Mar, 1733/37 ( the date of the will of John fi8shback) his first cousin, Ann Catherine Fishback, eldest daughter of John Fishback and his wife Agnes Haeger, 1714 immigrants, and granddaughter of P
2 CONC hilip & elizabeth (Heimbach) Fischbach and of Rev. Henry Haeger and his wife, Anna Catherine Friesenhagen. (Dr. Salmans gives March, 1731 as the date of the amrriage but do not know the source of this info.)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is an interesting problem regarding the date of death of Catherine, wife of John Rector. The Fishback Genealogy, which is usually quite accurate, states that she was born about 1714/15 at Germanna. The birth date is probably
2 CONC  quite correct, but the following deeds may indicate that "she was still living as late as 03 Jan 1789": (1) So far as this deed goes, the Catherine Rector involved could have been the widow of John Rector, Jr., son of John, Sr. a
2 CONC nd Catherine (Fishback) Rector, who died in the same year as his father, 1773. As we shall see, there is some reason to think that John Rector married his first cousin, Catherine, daughter of Henry Rector, Sr. In his will Henry le
2 CONC ft a bequest to his daughter, Catherine Rector, which was to go,in case of her death, to her daughter, Polly Rector, showing that Catherine had married a Rector. No other Rector seems to fit in as her husband except John Rector, J
2 CONC r. who died in 1773. However, the following deeds may indicate that the Catherine Rector, widow, of 1789 was the elder Catherine, widow of John Rector, Sr. ~from the book of The Germanna Records (corrections to the book in Burgurn
2 CONC dy). April 1963
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Anna Catherina Fischbach was born about 1714, in Germantown, Orange County, Virginia. She was the daughter of Johannes Fischbach and Agnes Haeger. Anna married Johannes Richter 11 Mar 1773; in Rectortown, Fauquier County, Virginia
2 CONC . Anna Catherina Richter passed away about 1775, in Rectortown, Fauquier County, Virginia.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Fischbach-168 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 15 2021, 18:15:59 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Fischbach (was/is) Family name from Germany.   As many others it was changed a few years after arriving in America to “Fishback”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna 'Catherina' died "after 03 January 1789". Wife of 'John' Johannes Ritcher/Rector. Daughter of Johannes 'John' Fischbach and Agnes Haeger Fischbach. Last name Fischbach to Fishback. Anna Catherina and her husband John Rector/R
2 CONC itcher were cousins and were married about 1732.  They had at least 10 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ++John Rector married prior to 11 Mar, 1733/37 ( the date of the will of John Fishback/Fischbach) his first cousin, Ann Catherine Fishback(Fischbach), eldest daughter of John Fishback and his wife Agnes Haeger, 1714 immigrants, an
2 CONC d granddaughter of Philip & Elizabeth (Heimbach) Fischbach and of Rev. Henry Haeger and his wife, Anna Catherine Friesenhagen. (Dr. Salmans gives March, 1731 as the date of the marriage but do not know the source of this info.)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is an interesting problem regarding the date of death of Catherine, wife of John Rector. The Fishback/Fischbach Genealogy, which is usually quite accurate, states that she was born about 1714/15 at Germanna. The birth date i
2 CONC s probably quite correct, but the following deeds may indicate that "she was still living as late as 03 Jan 1789":  (1) So far as this deed goes, the Catherine Rector involved could have been the widow of John Rector, Jr., son of 
2 CONC John, Sr. and Catherine (Fishback) Rector, who died in the same year as his father, 1773. As we shall see, there is some reason to think that John Rector married his first cousin, Catherine, daughter of Henry Rector, Sr. In his wi
2 CONC ll Henry left a bequest to his daughter, Catherine Rector, which was to go, in case of her death, to her daughter, Polly Rector, showing that Catherine had married a Rector. No other Rector seems to fit in as her husband except Jo
2 CONC hn Rector, Jr. who died in 1773. However, the following deeds may indicate that the Catherine Rector, widow, of 1789 was the elder Catherine, widow of John Rector, Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~from the book of ‘The Germanna Records’ (corrections to the book in Burgurndy). April 1963
2 CONT
2 CONT
