1 NOTE {geni:about_me} His name is not Johann or Johann Henrich, it's Johannes, no middle name. His parents are Johannes Hofmann born in 1663 in Eisern and baptised on 19 Jul 1663 and married Gertrud Reichmann 24 May 1690 in Siegen.  He 
2 CONC was not a Palatinate farmer, he was a Fuhrmann, a traveling dealer in iron products.  Gertrud Reichmann was born in 1666 in Siegen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Hofmann, Sr., died in 1737 in Eisern and his wife, Gertrud, died in 1728 in Eisern, both of them buried there.  They had 9 children, one of them, Johannes Hofmann, was born in 1692, he immigrated to Virginia in 1713 as a 
2 CONC bachelor later marrying Agnes Katharina Haeger on 7 Nov 1721 in Virginia.  Agnes Katharina Haeger is the daughter of Rev. Johann Henrich/Henry Haeger and his wife, Anna Catharina Friesenhagen.  Johannes/John and Agnes had 5 childr
2 CONC en, Agnes dying in childbirth, along with the baby, 9 Feb 1729.  
2 CONT
2 CONT John married as his second wife, Maria Sabina Charlotta Barbara Volck, a member of the 1717/Second Germanna Colony.  She was born in 1710 in Wagenbach, Hüffenhardt, Baden (now Baden-Württemberg, Germany) and immigrated to Virginia
2 CONC  with her mother, Anna Barbara (Majer) Utz, and her step father, Johann Georg Utz.  Maria Sabina's father, Johann Michael Volck, had died on 7 Apr 1714 in Wagenbach.  Maria Sabina and John Hofman had 12 children, all very well doc
2 CONC umented in the Germanna Foundation Database as well as the following publications:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://germannafamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I056720&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. BC Holtzclaw, Germanna Record No. 5: Ancestry and Descendants of the Nassau Siegen Immigrants to Virginis 1714-1750, (Culpeper, VA: The Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, Inc., 1964),339-361.
2 CONT
2 CONT Germanna Record #3: John Hoffman, 1714 Germanna Colonist and His Descendants, B.C. Holtzclaw, (Culpeper, VA: Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, April 1963, reprinted July 1989), 7.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hoffman: Records from his Bible, 1663-1813, (Beyond Germanna, 11, no. 2, (March 1999): 613), 613.
2 CONT
2 CONT  John Hoffman of Germanna and Some of His Descendants, John W. Wayland, (The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography, 63, no. 4, (October 1955): 454-460), 455.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hoffman, John W. Wayland from the John Hoffman Bible, (Annual Journal for the Society of Germanna Colonies, 1, no. 4 &5, (June 1953)), 40.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Price, Trustee/Genealogist
2 CONT The Germanna Foundation
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Johann Hoffman''' was born and baptized on March 8, 1692 in Siegen, Siegen-Wittgenstein, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, Siegen, Nassau Siegen, Westphalia, Germany. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34776627710 Johannes Hofmann] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-67235806 Gertrude Hofman]. He was a Palatinate farmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann married [https://www.geni.com/profile-20241125 Maria Sabina Charlotta Barbara Hofmann] on July 13, 1729 in Culpeper, Culpeper County, Virginia, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hoffman/6000000108301548173?through=6000000005229578490;
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-127901566 Nicholas Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34692562924 Michael Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34626286306 Paul Balthazar 'Baltz' Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-18126789 William Huffman, Sr.]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-26006421 Mary 'Maria' Hanback]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34728173280 Johann 'Jacob' Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34658522903 Jarg (George) Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34776631967 Frederick Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34626286477 Henry Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34626286549 Tilman Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34776631975 Elizabeth Back]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-67312949 Margaret Hoffman]. .
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann married [https://www.geni.com/profile-45090906 Anna Katharina Hofmann] on November 7, 1721 in Fauquier County, Virginia, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-67235624 Agnes Hofmann]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743092018 Anna Catharine Spilman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-46258758 John Hoffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743092026 Unnamed Son Hoffman, stillborn]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on July 3, 1772 in Culpeper, Culpeper County, Virginia, United States and was buried in July 1772. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://germannafamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I056720&tree=tree1
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hoffman-9438
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Virginia, United States - 1714
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Orange, North Carolina, United States - 1752
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LZJQ-2F1 FamilySearch Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 13 2021, 17:25:33 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was born in Siegen, Germany, although he and his family lived in Eisern, Germany. His parents were Johannes Hoffman (born 7-27-1663, and died 3-16-1731) and Gertrud Reichmann (died 9-25-1778), the daughter of John Reichman.
2 CONT
2 CONT He sailed to America in 1714. He settled in Germanna, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anna Catherine Haeger, on November 7, 1721. She was the daughter of Rev. Henry Haeger and Anna Katherine Friesenhagen.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Anna had five children: Agnes (born Nov. 25, 1722); John Henry (born Jan. 18, 1724); Anna Catherine (born June 7, 1725); John (born May 6, 1727); and an unnamed son stillborn (Feb. 9, 1729). John's wife Anna died during t
2 CONC he birth of their stillborn son.
2 CONT
2 CONT John got remarried to Maria Sabina Folg, on July 13, 1729. She was the daughter of John Michael Folg.  
2 CONT
2 CONT As soon as he married her, they left Germanna and moved to some land about 30 miles to the west, along the Robinson River. Several other men and their families went with them. This land was first in Culpeper County, Virginia, but 
2 CONC in 1792, it became Madison County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Maria had twelve children: Nicholas (born Feb. 4, 1731); Michael (born March 26, 1732); Jacob (born Dec. 3, 1733); Baltz, also known as Paul (born May 13, 1735); William (born Dec. 8, 1737); George (born April 10, 1739); 
2 CONC Frederick (born Feb. 7, 1740); Henry (born May 25, 1742); Tilman (born June 1, 1744); Elizabeth (born July 13, 1746); Margaret (born Nov. 27, 1748); and Mary (born Aug. 4, 1751). 
2 CONT
2 CONT John kept a family Bible, in which he listed the names and dates of birth of his two wives, and the names and dates of birth of all of his children. His Bible was actually just four pieces of blue-tinted paper, that were 5"x8" in 
2 CONC size. It has been transcribed and is shown on this memorial.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He wrote the name of his daughter Elizabeth into the Bible, with her date of birth, which was July 13, 1746. Her name and her date of birth were also written into the old Bach Family Bible, owned by Johann Heinrich Bach (John Hen
2 CONC ry Back), who was a close neighbor of John Hoffman. Johann Heinrich Bach's son Henry married John Hoffman's daughter Elizabeth, and so he wrote her name and date of birth into his Bach Family Bible, during the Christmas holiday of
2 CONC  1787. This proves that she married into his family, and not the family of Hermann Bach from Freudenberg, Germany.  (Elizabeth's sister Margaret married Henry's brother John. And Henry and John's brother Joseph married Elizabeth H
2 CONC offman-Maggard, who had been adopted by the Maggard family after she was orphaned in 1770.)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hoffman owned 3,525 acres of land. He wrote his will on Dec. 30, 1762. He left each of his four daughters 150 acres, and he left each of his sons land as well. Nine of them got 292 acres, and one of them (George) got 297 acre
2 CONC s with a mill (probably built by Johann Heinrich Bach).
2 CONT
2 CONT He probably died in the summer of 1772, as his will was probated on August 17, 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/167919529/john-hoffman Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 13 2021, 17:29:04 UTC''
2 CONT
