1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''John Hoffman''' was born on May 6, 1727 in Germantown, Fauquier County, Virginia, Colonial America. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-64732647 Johannes Hofmann] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-45090906 Anna Katha
2 CONC rina Hofmann (Haeger)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664278356 Alse Hoffman (Fishback)]. Together they had the following 8 known children:
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Huffman/6000000186267618087?through=6000000002906988689;
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-46254168 Christena Fishback (Hoffman)];
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Rev-Daniel-Huffman/6000000175960948104?through=6000000002906988689;
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Rev-James-Huffman/6000000175960948219?through=6000000002906988689;
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Huffman/6000000175960948117?through=6000000002906988689;
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Reuben-Huffman/6000000175960948124?through=6000000002906988689;
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Sampson-Huffman/6000000175960947873?through=6000000002906988689;
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-46258755 Samuel Hoffman].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on March 4, 1813 in Madison County, Virginia, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 	
2 CONT 12 May 1779 John Huffman signed petition requesting Culpeper County be divided into three separate counties ("Inhabitants: Petition," Culpeper County, 12 May 1779, Legislative Petitions Digital Collection, Library of Virginia, Ric
2 CONC hmond, VA. Legislative Petitions of the General Assembly, 1776-1865, Accession Number 36121, Box 317, Folder 5. Library of Virginia, (https://www.lva.virginia.gov/: accessed 9 April 2019), Virginia Memory > Digital Collections > C
2 CONC ollections A to Z > Legislative Petitions Digital Collection.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Madison County, Virginia Will Book 2: 410
2 CONT
