2 CONT
2 CONT "FAUQUIER DURING THE PROPRIETORSHIP" by H.C. Groome
2 CONT
2 CONT p.106) JOHN RECTOR: "Another descendant of Germantown, who, as will ap pear, laid off upon it the village now know as RECTORTOWN".
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently John received a land grant passed to him from Tilman Weaver, w ho "also made an investment of land in this locality in 1741, taking, o n March 26th of that year, 539 ac. on some of the branches of Crummey's r un adj. Ba
2 CONC ll's land." [E:240]
2 CONT
2 CONT p.130) "Wills of the founders of Germantown were proved as follows: ... . JOHN RECTOR (son of Jacob) March 22, 1773, (Kemper, Genealogy, etc., p . 52 and F.H. S. Bulletin, No. 4, p. 483)".
2 CONT
2 CONT # Birth: BEF 1 DEC 1711 in Trupbach, Siegen, Nordheim-Westfalen, GER
2 CONT
