2 CONT
2 CONT Fauquier County records show that John Rector was active in acquiring lar
2 CONT
2 CONT ge tracts of land, settling them in communities and then selling them to o
2 CONT
2 CONT thers. He sold his old land near Germantown before moving to the Northe
2 CONT
2 CONT rn part of the County. He would be the founder of Rectortown, VA. Immigara
2 CONT
2 CONT ted to VA in 1714. His brother Harmon was mentioned in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some genealogist have John married in Rectortown, Fauquier Co., VA, to Cat
2 CONT
2 CONT herine or Katherine TAYLOR, pos born 2 Jul 1707 in North Farnham Parish, V
2 CONT
2 CONT A. This would make her the mother of all but the first one to three childr
2 CONT
2 CONT en. If they were married abt 1737. as many as three would have been bo
2 CONT
2 CONT rn to Anna, with the rest born to Katherine. I've seem that some genealogi
2 CONT
2 CONT st also have found that a Mary Spilman was married into the family, whi
2 CONT
2 CONT ch would explain some confusion. I still find some confusion, that I haven
2 CONT
2 CONT 't been able to sort out yet. Dates of the children by Mary Spillman confl
2 CONT
2 CONT ict with dates of other children by wives. Perhaps, from looking at the co
2 CONT
2 CONT nfusion, a John from New York, came down to Virginia and married Mar
2 CONT
2 CONT y. It seems that Hans translated John ofcourse may have been part of John
2 CONT
2 CONT 's brother Jacob's name. Hans commonly given to more than one child in th
2 CONT
2 CONT is family as a patron saint. Common in German naming patterns, with the ch
2 CONT
2 CONT ildren going by their other name. Could she actually have been marri
2 CONT
2 CONT ed to Jacob? Jacob is married to a Mary that seems confused with Mary Hi
2 CONT
2 CONT tt unlikely being attributed to at least three of the Rector men in this f
2 CONT
2 CONT amily (dates of the children don't allow a couple of the relationships, ev
2 CONT
2 CONT en though it was common enough for someone to marry back into the same fam
2 CONT
2 CONT ily at that time). More analytical research needed on the proofs with a co
2 CONT
2 CONT mparison of the different pieces to the puzzle being compared.
2 CONT
