2 CONT          Will probated 24 March 1773, Fauquier County, Virginia
2 CONT          Will Book #1 page 205
2 CONT The Prince William County records show Elizabeth (Rector) had four sons instead
2 CONT of two.  Prince William County Rent Rolls of 1753 and 1754 show Harman Rector,
2 CONT Henry Rector, and Jacob Rector each with 100 Acres of land.  John Rector, the
2 CONT eldest brother is not shown in 1753, but 1754 shows him with 300 acres in John
2 CONT Baylis's List. We know from the deeds that the last three sons were born
2 CONT between 1715 to 1725.  All records have been searched to try to find birthdates
2 CONT for these sons, but none have been found.
2 CONT #1 John, will was probated 24 Mar. 1773 Fauquier Co. Va. Will Book 1 pg 205
2 CONT #2 Harman, will was probated 28 Sept. 1789 Fauquier Co. Va. Will Book 2 pg 147
2 CONT #3 Henry, will was probated 24 June 1799 Fauquier Co. Va. Will Book 3 pg 182
2 CONT #4 Jacob, will was probated July 1811 Grayson Co. Va. Will Book 1 pg 77
