1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Atwood died soon after the birth of his daughter Elizabeth in 1799. His widow "Caty" appears in the Culpeper County personal tax list in 1800, with 2 white males 16+, 2 slaves 16+, and 2 slaves 12-16.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 Aug. 1802, James Atwood's four eldest (adult) children, with three spouses, sold 142 acres of land in Culpeper County to Samuel Wood for £200; this was apparently part of the settlement of his estate.
