1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Harnsberger 
2 CONT * Birth:	1743 near Port Royal, Rockingham, Virginia, United States
2 CONT * Death:	July 1842 - Alleghany Co. VA
2 CONT * Parents:	Stephen Harnsberger, Agnes Hoffman
2 CONT * Siblings:	Barbara Mauck (born Harnsberger), Margaret Huffman (born Harnsberger), Adam Harnsberger, Henry Harnsberger, Stephen Harnsberger, Conrad Harnsberger, Robert Harnsberger, Elizabeth Lingle (born Harnsberger)
2 CONT * spouse(s) unknown
2 CONT * Father of Elizabeth Harnsberger, Jacob Harnsberger, Nancy Harnsberger, Rebecca Harnsberger, Sally Harnsberger, Sebastian Harnsberger and John III Harnsberger
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Harnsberger was apparently in the bad graces of his father, when John Harnsberger made his Will in 1760, as no mention of his second marriage was made in the document, except indirectly by the mention of Stephen's children
2 CONC  "by his first wife, Agnes", we know that Stephen was married again and that his second wife's name was Ursula Shitley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later in the will, John directed that the plantation be divided, after the decease of his wife , 1/2 to '''John, son of Stephen''', and the remaining half to Stephen's three daughters, Barbara, Elizabeth and Margaret
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1775 Stephen wrote his will in the presence of John Zimmerman, George Zimmerman, Adam Carpenter, Jacob Miller, and Conrad Zimmerman. Though all of these names are Germanna names, the individuals themselves are believed to have 
2 CONC sources other than Germanna. The will was proved in 1776 in Augusta County. Only the wife Ursula and sons, Adam, Henry, Stephen, Conrad, and Robert are mentioned.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
