1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Joseph Huffman''' was born between 1750 and 1754. His parents were https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hoffman/6000000002906988689 and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664278356 Alse Hoffman (Fishback)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34777793984 Elizabeth Huffman ({unknown})]. Together they had the following 5 known children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34777793986 George Huffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34777793987 Polly Huffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34777793990 Leanah Huffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34777793992 Henry Huffman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34777793994 Moses Huffman]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1837 in Madison County, Virginia, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Huffman served in the Revolutionary War (Germanna Record No. 5: Ancestry and Descendants of the Nassau Siegen Immigrants to Virginia 1714-1750, 364, cites Gwathmey's "Historical Register of Virginians in the Revolution," 38
2 CONC 2, 399.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Madison County, Virginia 1810 Federal Census, p 356/389: Huffman, Joseph - 1 male age 0-9, 1 male age 10-15, 1 male age 45 and over, 2 females age 16-25, 2 females age 45 and over, 1 slave
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 	
2 CONT # [S0040277] Germanna Record #3: John Hoffman, 1714 Germanna Colonist and His Descendants, B.C. Holtzclaw, (Culpeper, VA: Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, April 1963, reprinted July 1989), 13.
2 CONT named in his father's will
2 CONT # [S0040277] Germanna Record #3: John Hoffman, 1714 Germanna Colonist and His Descendants, B.C. Holtzclaw, (Culpeper, VA: Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, April 1963, reprinted July 1989), 14.
2 CONT about 1750-1754, 17 c1752-4
2 CONT # [S0040278] Germanna Record No. 5: Ancestry and Descendants of the Nassau-Siegen Immigrants to Virginia 1714-1750, B. C. Holtzclaw, (Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, 1964, Sixth Printing 2002), 343.
2 CONT about 1750-1751
2 CONT # [S0040277] Germanna Record #3: John Hoffman, 1714 Germanna Colonist and His Descendants, B.C. Holtzclaw, (Culpeper, VA: Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, April 1963, reprinted July 1989), 14.
2 CONT will written 23 July 1834, probated 27 Nov 1837, 17
