1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daniel Myers, a New York Loyalist whose family came from the Palatinate region of Germany. He was the original builder of the house that later became the historic Willard's Hotel, which is now a national attraction
2 CONC  at Upper Canada Village in South Dundas Township along the St. Lawrence River in Ontario. The original house was also used as an inn. It was known to travelers as the "Halfway House" because it was located centrally between Cornw
2 CONC all and Prescott.
