2 DATA
3 DATE 29 APR 2020
3 TEXT First Name
3 TEXT Birth: 	Mar. 10, 1764
4 CONT Fauquier County
4 CONT Virginia, USA
4 CONT Death: 	Feb. 5, 1856
4 CONT
4 CONT married 1st Chloe McPherson 29 Sept 1786 and 2nd Rebecca Sevier
4 CONT
4 CONT Revolutionary War soldier who served under General George Rogers Clark. John Rector DAR Ancestor #A094505.
4 CONT
4 CONT In memory of John Rector,
4 CONT Was born March 10, 1764
4 CONT Died February 5, 1856
4 CONT
4 CONT Index to Wills - Book 1
4 CONT 1828 - 1873
4 CONT Greene Co., Tennessee
4 CONT Rector, John 452
4 CONT
4 CONT children listd per will:
4 CONT by 1st marriage
4 CONT Nelly Irving
4 CONT Deborah Whillock
4 CONT Nancy Hulse
4 CONT Rachel Howard
4 CONT Elizabeth Dunlap
4 CONT Sarah Guinn
4 CONT Mary Kibler
4 CONT Enoch Rector
4 CONT
4 CONT children by 2nd marriage
4 CONT John Rector
4 CONT George Rector
4 CONT Franklin Rector
4 CONT Jane Rector
4 CONT Harriet Peters
4 CONT Susan Dearstone
4 CONT Mariah Roberts
4 CONT Rebecca Peters
4 CONT ***
4 CONT Tennessee, Probate Court Books, 1795-1927 Greene Wills, 1828-1873, Vol. 01
4 CONT Pg 452 and 453
4 CONT March 3rd 1856 min'ts 22 page 256
4 CONT
4 CONT I John Rector Senr. of the County of Greene and State of Tennessee, do make and publish this as my last Will and Testament, Hereby revoking and making void all other Wills by me at any tie made.
4 CONT
4 CONT First I direct that my funeral expenses and all my debts be paid as soon after my death as possible out of any money that I may die possessed of or may first come into the hands of my Executor.
4 CONT
4 CONT Secondly To each of my children by first marriage I give and bequeath the Some of one dollar namely Nelly Irving, Deborah Whillock, Nancy Hults, Rachel Howard, Elizabeth Dunlap, Sarah Guinn, Mary Kibler and Enoch Rector.
4 CONT
4 CONT Thirdly to my Son John Rector and his heirs forever I will and devise the tract of land he now lives on containing fifty acres more or less.
4 CONT
4 CONT Fourthly To my two Sons George Rector and Franklin Rector and their Heirs forever to be divided equally I give and devise the tract of land or place I now live.
4 CONT
4 CONT Fifthly I also give and bequeath to my Son George Rector my Brown mare, one beadstead bed and furniture and Six chairs.
4 CONT
4 CONT Sixthly I give and bequeath to my daughter Jane Rector one bedstead good bed and furniture all my cupboard or Table ware one pot one oven one Skillet and one pare of pot hooks One Bureau and one half round Table.
4 CONT
4 CONT Seventhly I also give to my daughter Jane Rector one Bay filly two years old this Spring.
4 CONT
4 CONT Eighthly I direct that my Executor Sell at public Sale on twelve months credit all my Stock and property of every description not above named and when the money is collected, to pay it over to my daughters by my last marriage, to 
4 CONC wit, Susan Dearstone, Harriet Peters, Mariah Roberts, Rebecca Peters and Jane Rector, equally, and the debts and accounts due me I wish collected without delay and the same paid over to my last named Daughters Susan, Harriet, Mari
4 CONC a, Rebecca and Jane, equally.
4 CONT
4 CONT Ninthly I give and bequeath to my three Sons John Rector, George Rector and Franklin Rector One hundred dollars each out of the money that is now in the hands of George Jones and the balance if any to be equally divided between my
4 CONC  daughters Susan, Harriet, Maria, Rebecca and Jane.
4 CONT
4 CONT Lastly I do hereby nominate and appoint John Davis my Executor.
4 CONT
4 CONT In witness whereof I set my hand and seal this 16th day of March 1853.
4 CONT John (X) Rector Sr
4 CONT
4 CONT Signed Sealed and published in our 
4 CONT presence and we have Subscribed our names hereto in the presence of the Testator this 16th day of March 1853.
4 CONT Test
4 CONT A. J. Rhea
4 CONT Isaac Basinger
4 CONT ***
4 CONT
4 CONT Washington County Court Records, Box 3, Folder 159, Superior Court, ETSU, 16 Sept 2011 researched by Carolyn Whitaker (transcribed as written)
4 CONT Agreement between JOHN MILLIKEN & JOHN RECTOR, dated 29 Aug 1796
4 CONT Articles of an agreement maid and inter'd upon this twenty ninth day of august one thousand seven hundred and ninty six, between JOHN MILLIKEN off the one part and JOHN RECTOR off the other part--
4 CONT
4 CONT the said MILLIKEN hath given into the hands of the said RECTOR on a commifsion fore defrent surveys off land; containg in the whole 330.00 acres.
4 CONT
4 CONT Lying in the cty of Wafhington and Green on the WATERS OF CHUCKEY RIVER. -
4 CONT
4 CONT the sd MILLIKEN gives the said RECTOR half the sum the land or lands may be sold for by the sd RECTOR. The said MILLIKEN is to be at half The expence that may arise in the time of negotiating the sales of said land or lands. The s
4 CONC aid RECTOR is to be on oath off requested what the espencies amts to.--
4 CONT
4 CONT the said RECTOR is to Deliver what ever the land or lands be sold for or one half that To the said MILLIKEN in some village or villages in the state of Tennefee--
4 CONT
4 CONT With the said MILLIKENS discharging the expencies that may arise from the moaving the property to and from the certain place or places. the said RECTOR Is to be on oath if requrd when and what he the said RECTOR got and sold The l
4 CONC and or lands for. the said MILLIKEN is To have what ever the land or lands or his part theroff may sell for. at the first cost will his defraying the expencies as above mentioned for the true performance wheroff, we bind our selve
4 CONC s heires Executors and administators in the penal sum off Twenty thousand sponis? milld dollrs in testimoney we have herunto set our hands and seales this twenty Ninth day off August 1796
4 CONT
4 CONT JOHN MILLIKEN (seal)
4 CONT JOHN RECTOR (seal)
4 CONT
