2 CONT DAR Lineage Book Vol. 117, 1915, pgs 195-196: "Miss Mary Lee Glascock - 16630 Born in Maysville, Ky. Desc. of Lieut. Thomas Glascock and of William Asbury, as follows: 1. Arthur Lee Glascock (b. 1868) m. 1892 Sophia Adelaide _____
2 CONC  (b. 1867). 2. Albert Rector Glascock (b. 1834) m. 1866 Anne Elizabeth Parks (b. 1842). 3. Thomas Glascock (1796-1872) m. 1815 Elizabeth Asbury (1799-1880). 4. George Glascock (1777-1832) m. Frances Jackson (1769-1853); William As
2 CONC bury m 1784 Susan Glascock (1757-1857). 5. Thomas Glascock m Caty Rector.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Glascock (1757-1840) in 1777 was lieutenant of a Geargia regiment; also lieutenant of Continental Dragoons, 1779. He was born in Fauquier County, Va.; died in Virginia. William Asbury served two years in the Revolution; eng
2 CONC aged in the battles of Cowpens, Guilford Court House and Yorktown. His widow was granted a pension. He was born in Virginia; died, 1814, in Fleming, Ky."
