1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Glascock/6000000007699137352?through=6000000002702742593 who married https://www.geni.com/people/John-Glascock-Sr/6000000007698742443?through=6000000007699137352
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT Updated 21 April 2024
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mary Glasscock''', daughter of John Glasscock (d. 1784) & Margaret O’Rear, was born 30 Jul 1734 in Fauquier County, Virginia Colony.  Mary was named “my daughter '''Mary Richter'''” in [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Glascock
2 CONC -Sr/6000000016349881407?through=6000000002906180404 John Glasscock’s] 1780  Will.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She died as '''Mary Gore''' on 22 May 1822 at age 87 in Rectortown, Fauquier, Virginia, United States.  She is buried in the Rectortown Cemetery.   A gravestone could not be found for her. The gravestones have not weathered well a
2 CONC nd ones from mid 1800's are barely legible.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (born Glasscock) married three times. 
2 CONT
2 CONT First, at age 25, to John Glascock  on November 28, 1759 [NO - that’s the marriage date for https://www.geni.com/people/John-Glasscock-Sr/6000000007698742443?through=6000000007699137352 & https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Glasscock
2 CONC /6000000007699137352?through=6000000007698742443] .   They had one daughter together. She was named  “my wife Mary” in his Will written 8 March 1765, “to receive half his estate.  Daughter Frances to receive the other half.”
2 CONT
2 CONT This John Glasscock was the son of Gregory Glascock and Elizabeth Elder. His brother Gregory Glasscock witnessed his will.  His brother in law [https://www.geni.com/people/Lt-Thomas-Glasscock/6000000002520136305?through=6000000002
2 CONC 906180404 Thomas Glasscock], Mary’s brother, was an executor, along with his wife.  See [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000205230178890 attached document]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After he died Mary, now age 31, married Henry Rector in 1765, the son of John and Catherine (Taylor) Rector. They had at least six children together. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After he died in 1781, Mary  (age 47) married Joshua Gore. She is called “my wife” in his 1785 Will: “ to my wife a bay mare which I got from Timothy Howell last Fall and two cows... to my wife the sheep which she brought on this 
2 CONC plantation... to my wife all the goods and effects whatsoever I became possessed of in consequence of my marriage with her and effects which she became possessed of by the death of her former husband, Harry Rector... excepting suc
2 CONC h articles as I have paid for to the Ex'ors of Harry Rector's Estate...
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no record of Joshua Gore and Mary having children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the will of Mary Gore  written 28 Sep 1813 and probated 27 May 1822 in Fauquier Co., VA, she named her son, Enoch RECTOR, her nephew Enoch GLASSCOCK, and her daughters, Peggy GORE, Frances GODARD, Elizabeth SHACKLETT and Catter
2 CONC en GLASSCOCK. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Disambiguation 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Glasscock) RECTOR GORE (this profile)  married Henry RECTOR in 1756.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Hendren) GLASSCOCK married John GLASSCOCK, Jr in 1759. These are two different women. Mary (Glasscock) RECTOR GORE is the sister of John GLASSCOCK, Jr and the sister-in-law of Mary (Hendren) GLASSCOCK (?).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
