1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LEWIS RECTOR was born about 1765 in Fauquier County, Virginia. He later moved to Campbell County, Virginia. He later moved in Roane County, Tennessee.  Lewis was a farmer. Lewis died about 1830 in Oliver Springs, R
2 CONC oane County, Tennessee. He is probably buried in the Oliver Springs, Tennessee area. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis Rector, Senior bought twenty-one acres from Moses Winters of his original 249 acre tract. Lewis either remodeled a crude house, or he built the big sturdy log house at the corner of Main and Spring Streets, and presently occ
2 CONC upied by Mrs. Geraldine Blanton of Oliver Spring, Tennessee. The house is on the National Register. (Source: Roane County Deed Book E, Page 409; December 23, 1819)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Jacob Rector (1740-1779) & Jane.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT #SARAH BUTLER, the daughter of WILLIAM BUTLER, SENIOR and ANN DUCKETT, in March 1792 in Campbell County, Virginia.  Sarah died in Campbell County, Virginia in 1798. Charles Rock was accused of having poisoned her and the trial is 
2 CONC recorded in Campbell County.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Martin - d Bef 1817 m. 14 Jan 1799
2 CONT #Elizabeth Moore m. 16 May 1817
2 CONT
2 CONT He had children by all three wives.
2 CONT ----
