1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was the son of Jacob Rector (1740-1779) & Jane.
2 CONT
2 CONT The settlement of Martin Rector's estate went as follows: William C Kington and Rhody his wife, David Summers and Charlotte his wife of Morgan County, Tennessee, Matthew Williams and Judy his wife of Rhea County, Tennessee, Isaac 
2 CONC England and Rebecca his wife of McCoupin County, Illinois, were heirs of Martin Rector, dec'd formerly of Morgan County,Tennessee. Martin Rector had son, David M and daughter, Polly, both minors. Martin died March 11, 1832 leaving
2 CONC  besides his children, a widow named Sarah. Richard Oliver was administrator of his estate. December term 1833. pp. 725 - 729.
2 CONT
