1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://germannafamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I081367&tree=tree1
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://www.geocities.ws/pvorenberg/photoHMRector.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Rector [Frederick (1750-1811), John (1711- 1777), Hans Jacob (1674-1729)] was the first of the Rectors  who came to the state or Arkansas (or territory then) , about 1818 as a surveyor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had been in Missouri and Illinois previously, and was one of nine brothers, born in Fauquier County, Virginia, several of whom went westward with the tide of immigration then sweeping into the Missouri Valley.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Rector served as Colonel of the Illinois militia from 1812 to 1814, and later as postmaster at Saint Louis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He filed the first land claim in Hot Springs, January 17, 1819. In 1821 he was elected to State Senate of Missouri. 
2 CONT --------------------
