2 CONT ID: I8288 Name: Zachariah SMITH Surname: Smith Given Name: Zachariah Sex: M Birth: ABT 1735 in ,Orange,Va. Death: ABT 1816 in ,Mercer,Ky. _UID: FB822F907B41D511BD9EBDC3D79617316E9E Note: Zacharias moved to Kentucky about 1777 with
2 CONC  other individuals from Germanna, including his brothers Adam and John. He was in the church records fairly often up to the year 1777 but he does not appear after that year in the church records. Suggestions have been made that hi
2 CONC s wives were Anne Elizabeth Fishback, the first wife, and Sarah Anne Watts. I believe it is correct that we would like better proof of both of these women.
2 CONT
2 CONT One other individual who moved at the time of Zacharias Smith was Jacob Holtzclaw, son of 1714 Jacob. Jacob (Jr.) married Susanna Thomas, the sister of Barbara Thomas who had married Jacob Blankenbaker. These women were daughters 
2 CONC of John Thomas (Jr.) and granddaughters of Anna Maria (nee) Blankenbaker. Henry Blankenbaker and the wife of Jacob Holtzclaw, Jr. were first cousins. John Blankenbaker says he raised a crop of corn in Ky. in 1776. Secnd wife was S
2 CONC arah Ann Watts. The thirteen hundred and seventy-first note in a series on the Germanna  Colonies  Zachariah Smith was the son of J. Michael Smith (Jr.) and was possibly born  around 1735. He died in Mercer Co., KY about 1816. He 
2 CONC married Ann Elizabeth  Fishback, the daughter of John Frederick Fishback and his wife, Ann  Elizabeth Holtzclaw. Therefore, she had two ancestors in the First Germanna  Colony. There is a record that they were sponsors for the bap
2 CONC tism of a  child in 1767. She probably died not too long after this time. When  Zachariah sold land in 1777, his wife was Sarah Ann. Probably they were  married around 1770 for they had a daughter who married William Smith in  178
2 CONC 8. The parentage of Sarah Ann is not proven.  There is a record that Zacharias raised a crop of corn in 1776 in Kentucky  Co., (later Lincoln and finally Mercer Co., KY) and took out land rights in  1779-80. Zacharias served in th
2 CONC e Revolutionary War in a detachment of  Lincoln Co. militia under the command of Ensign John Smith who may have  been his brother. These records are identical to those of Jacob Holtzclaw,  the son of the 1714 colonist, who married
2 CONC  Susanna, daughter of John Thomas,  Jr. Susanna was Zacharias' first cousin as John Thomas, Jr. and Anna  Magdalena Thomas Smith were brother and sister.  A series of deeds in Kentucky furnishes some clues as to the children of  Z
2 CONC acharias. '''By his first wife, Ann Elizabeth Fishback: 1. William Smith (he left seven children), 2. Elizabeth Smith m. Capt. Henry Grider of Swiss Mennonite descent, 3. Mary Smith m. William Powell, 4. Jesse Smith m. Joanna Pend
2 CONC leton'''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By his second wife, Sarah Ann, these children resulted: 5. Zachariah Smith, Jr. m. Elizabeth, 6. Peter Smith m. Elizabeth, 7. Jeremiah Smith m. Polly, 8. James Smith m. Margaret, 9. Samuel Smith, 10. Abraham Smith m. Nancy, 11.
2 CONC  Sally Smith m.1 a cousin, William Smith and m.2 Uriah Taylor.''' Since  Sally Smith had a daughter who was married in 1788, Sally was probably one  of the older children of the second marriage. (Zachariah Smith and Elijah  Holtzc
2 CONC law were on the marriage bond.) This continues to show the close  connection of the Smiths and Holtzclaws. 12. Mildred Smith m. Joseph Fisher. 13. Nancy Smith m. Robert Ragan.  Sarah Browder, who descends from this family, is not 
2 CONC entirely convinced of  these points. There are numerous uncertainties.  John Blankenbaker   Census: 1810, Mercer Co., KY- male and female over age 45 pg 332 Church Membership 1: 1767,Culpeper Co., VA - Hebron Lutheran Church Zacha
2 CONC riah/Anna Schmidt were sponsorsfor Baptism of Julius Chrisler-his nephew Church Membership 2: 1769,Culpeper Co., VA - Hebron Lutheran Church Zachariah (no wife) was sponsor forBaptism of Elizabeth Christler, his niece Church Membe
2 CONC rship 3: 1771,Culpeper Co., VA - Hebron Lutheran Church Zachariah (no wife) was sponsor forBaptism of Abraham Christler, his nephew Church Membership 4: 1775,Culpeper Co., VA - Hebron Lutheran Church Zachariah (no wife) was sponso
2 CONC r forBaptism of Absolom Christler, his nephew Church Membership 5: 1777,Culpeper Co., VA -- Hebron Lutheran Church Zachariah was a sponsor for theBaptism of Elizabeth, d/o John Smith Jr/Elizabeth (his brother) County records 1: Be
2 CONC t. 1770- 1779, Culpeper Co., VA - signed legislative petitions in the 1770's on recordin the Virginia State Library, presumed to have been Minutemen. County records 2: March 16,1772, Culpeper Co., VA - Had adjoining land on deed f
