2 CONC re he lived, descended to his children and heirs at law. Joseph Fisher purchased a part of interest from heirs of William Smith, deceased  DB 13 page 191 January 18, 1824 Zachariah and Agnes Smith to Jesse Smith -- Zachariah Smith
2 CONC , father and ancestor to Zachariah and Jesse departed this life on the _______ day of 1816 leaving Jesse and Zachariah with Peter, Jeremiah R. James, Samuel, Abraham, Elizabeth Grider wife of Henry, Mary Powell, widow of William, 
2 CONC deceased, Sally Taylor, wife of Uriah, Milly Fisher, wife of Joesph, Nancy Ragan, wife of Robert and the heirs of William Smith, deceased son. Zachariah and Jesse have purchased all the tracts of Zachariah, deceased and have agree
2 CONC d to make a division among themselves.  So without these wonderful land records, we would never know the children of Zachariah Smith  Zachariah's estate recorded WB 5 page 349 in 1817 -- don't know why I did not make note of this 
2 CONC -- I did a few others -- oh well, another unfinished chore but the reference could be included in the following note:  I don't have the book and page for this record but have the note in my files  In 1817 Sarah Ann (Watts) Smith d
2 CONC eeded to Zachariah, James, and Jesse Smith, and to Joseph Fisher, Robert Ragan, and to Jeremiah, Samuel, and Abraham Smith of Garrard Co. all of rights in the land of her deceased husband, Zachariah, on condition that they pay her
2 CONC  $91 annually in accordance with notes that she holds from them. Sarah Ann did not die until 1835 and she mentions her daughter Nancy Ragan?s second son, Reuben G. Ragan. Zacharias Ragan, the eldest son of Nancy, was also mentione
2 CONC d. Three daughters were mentioned, Sally Taylor, Mildred Fisher, and Nancy Ragan. It is believed that all of these people were Sarah Ann?s own children.
