1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of the Fishback family in America, the descendants of John Fishback, the emigrant, with an historical sketch of his family and of the colony at Germanna and Germantown, Virginia, 1714-1914.   Kemper, Willis M Publication
2 CONC  date 1914.  Page 26.   [https://archive.org/details/genealogyoffishb00kemp/page/103/mode/1up?q=Amiss Archive.Org] 
2 CONT
2 CONT THIRD GENERATION. 103 
2 CONT
2 CONT 26 MARTIN FISHBACK.  (John Frederick, John.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT *B. "Fleetwood," Culpeper Co., Va., 12  Oct., 1763. 
2 CONT *D. same place, 24 Jany., 1842.  M. 23 Mch., 1783. 
2 CONT *Married Lucy Amiss,  dau. Wm. and Annie ( ) Amiss; b. 8  July, 1763; d. 12 Sept., 1843. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin was born, married, and died in the same room; was a Revolutionary soldier, and at the age of 17 was present at the  siege of Yorktown and surrender of Cornwallis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT * 103 I. Polly.*
2 CONT * 104 II. Elliott, b. 15 Oct., 1785; d. 7 Nov., 1814; n. m.
2 CONT * 105 III. William, b. 6 Apl., 1788; d. 30 Sept., 1812; m. 7 June, 1809, Ann Edwards, s. p., an M. D. supposed to be buried, Leesburg, Va.
2 CONT * 106 IV. Martin, b. 11 Feby., 1791; d. 4 Mch., 1815; n. m.
2 CONT * Nancy.t
2 CONT * Lucy, b. 28 Feby., 1796; d. 4 Oct., 1799.
2 CONT * Sally Hill.t
2 CONT * Susan M.f
2 CONT * Frederick.!
2 CONT * X. Judith Mitcham, b. 28 July, 1806; d. 8 Aug., 1820; n. m.; buried "Fleetwood."
2 CONT *  113 XL Samuel, d. while attending school in Phila- delphia.
2 CONT --------------------
