2 CONT ID: I10546 Name: George Nimrod KEMPER Surname: Kemper Given Name: George Nimrod Sex: M Birth: 5 Mar 1772 in Germantown,Fauquier,Va. Death: 15 Aug 1820 in ,Garrard,Ky. _UID: CD8B2F907B41D511BD9EBDC3D79617314945 Note: according to E
2 CONC velyn Wallace at hdanw@aol.com he went to Garrard Co. Ky in 1794. His wife was said to have been Nancy Kelly and he had 5 or 6 children. One of these was John Frederick Kemper b act 1802 and killed by Karankawa Indians in Victoria
2 CONC  Co. Tx/ in 1845. John Frederick came to Tx. in 1830's following his father's death to help fight in the Texas Revolution. He then married his commanding officer's daughter and had two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT George was buried on his father's farm, near Buena Vista, Garrard Co., K Y. Children John Frederick KEMPER b: 18 JUL 1802 in , Garrard Co.,KY (Kentucky Co,VA-1777; Lincoln Co,VA-1780; Lincoln Co,KY-1792; Garrard Co., KY-1797) Jame
2 CONC s KEMPER b: 27 FEB 1804 in , Garrard Co.,KY (Kentucky Co,VA-1777; Lincoln Co,VA-1780; Lincoln Co,KY-1792; Garrard Co., KY-1797) Hannah KEMPER b: ABT 1807 in , Garrard Co.,KY (Kentucky Co,VA-1777; Lincoln Co,VA-1780; Lincoln Co,KY-
2 CONC 1792; Garrard Co., KY-1797) Peter KEMPER b: 16 JAN 1810 in , Garrard Co.,KY (Kentucky Co,VA-1777; Lincoln Co,VA-1780; Lincoln Co,KY-1792; Garrard Co., KY-1797) Enoch KEMPER b: 20 AUG 1812 in , Garrard Co.,KY (Kentucky Co,VA-1777; 
2 CONC Lincoln Co,VA-1780; Lincoln Co,KY-1792; Garrard Co., KY-1797)
2 CONT
2 CONT  On page 382 of this same volume compiled by the Cooks, there is reference to a small frame house built by George N. Camper, located in Lexington "on Upper Street". (I have an ancestor named George Nimrod Kemper, later of Garrard 
2 CONC Co., KY. Wonder if this is the same person? But like all colonials and their descendants, families used the same given names over and over!!! And George Nimrod Kemper's father in Garrard Co. was -- what else?--John Kemper of Dicks
2 CONC  River area. There was a younger John Kemper in the southern part--with a wife believed to be Judith Burditt.)  E.W.Wallace Change Date: 4 Jul 2009 at 01:00:00
2 CONT
