1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [http://germannafamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I000916&tree=tree1 TNG Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 25 2021, 19:03:52 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nathan and his brothers Reuben and Samuel moved to the south in the beginnings of the 1800's.  They engaged in the border wars with Spanish-America and then settled in Louisiana.  Nathan moved to St. Mary Parish in 1807 and went i
2 CONC nto a partnership with Louisiana Governor Henry Johnson to open up a sugar plantation in Bayou Sale.  
2 CONT
2 CONT As a side note to the Kemper family they were brought from Germany to America in 1714 by Virginia Governor Alexander Spottswood to operate mines in that state.  John/Johannes Kemper settled in the little colony at Fort  Germanna i
2 CONC n Virginia with about 40 other people from the Siegerland ( currently the area of Siegen the south Westphalian part of North Rhine-Westphalia. It is located in the district of Siegen-Wittgenstein in the Arnsberg region of Germany.
2 CONC  )
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Louisiana: Comprising Sketches of Parishes, Towns, Events, Institutions, and Persons, Arranged in Cyclopedic Form. Edited by Alcee Fortier. Published 1914 by Century Historical Association. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT  Germanna.org
2 CONT ----
2 CONT  Genealogy of the Kemper family in the United States; descendants of John Kemper of Virginia; with a short historical sketch of his family and of the German Reformed colony at Germanna and Germantown, Va. Compiled and edited by Wi
2 CONC llis Miller Kemper and Harry Linn Wright. online : https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89066178740;view=1up;seq=5
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Wikipedia
