1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://germannafamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I061919&tree=tree1
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From Jaime Howley:  Elnathan was a school master. Elnathan gave the land from his family for Lane Seminary to be built.  Elnathan and his father succumbed in August 1834 during the first Cholera epidemic on the Ohio River. First w
2 CONC ife was Francis Kemper, a cousin. They had no surviving children.  Three of his daughters with Eleanore married ministers.  Probably all graduates of Lane Seminary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo by: Lisa Ryan, added 4/21/2013 to Find A Grave Memorial# 78970682
