2 CONT Madison County, Virginia A Revised History by Margaret G. Davis (Madison County Board of Supervisors, Madison VA 1977), p 91: Bethcar Baptist Church was formed in 1823 so members of Robinson River Regular Baptist Church living nea
2 CONC r Madison Court House would not have to travel so far to attend services. Among those withdrawing to form Bethcar were Moses Clore, Absalom Carpenter, Ephraim Clore, James W. Crow, John Fishback, Abner Deer, Margaret Clore and Ann
2 CONC a Fishback.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 August 1823 "The petition of Brother Michael Yeager for letters of dismissal to form a new Constitution as Beth Car Meeting House was granted and 57 members were dismissed by letter to form a new church under the guidance of Eld
2 CONC er Oliver Welch." Among the members dismissed were Anna Fishback, Elizabeth Fishback, and John Fishback (Beth Car Baptist Church, "About Us," (http://www.bethcarbaptist.com/aboutus.html: accessed 8 February 2010).
2 CONT John Fishback was acting as clerk of the Robison River Baptist Church. At the conclusion of the list of members dismissed to constitute the new church he wrote, "This is the last work I’ve done August 6th. John Fishback, Clerk." (
2 CONC Minutes of the Robinson River Baptist Church at Criglersville: unpaginated, Baptist Church of Christ Minutes of this, 1822-1881, Accession #4233, Albert and Shirley Small Special Collections Library, University of Virginia, Charlo
2 CONC ttesville, Va, microfilm viewed 10 July 2023.).
2 CONT
