2 CONT John Fishback 81 MFarmer $16,048/$12,530Va
2 CONT Ann " 77 F "
2 CONT Judy " 56 F "
2 CONT Staunton Fishback40 MMaster Machinist --/$5146Va
2 CONT Dicey E. " 17 F "
2 CONT George W. Jackwson 15 MApp"
2 CONT Andrew J. Carpenter 14 M " "
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of John Fishback was written 1 November 1857 and proved 22 August 1861. He names wife Ann, son Staunton, Talitha Carpenter's sons Albert and John, and Joel M. Clore (relationship not given). Wheelwrights shop sold to son 
2 CONC Staunton. The following were to have one-tenth part of the estate: Judith Fishback; children of Elizabeth Wilson, deceased; Cave Fishback; Peacha Wilson; Talitha Carpenter; William M. Fishback; Waller Fishback; Saunton Fishback; M
2 CONC argaret Gooding, wife of John R. Gooding; and Mary Ann Clore, wife of Joel M. Clore. A codicil dated 20 April 1860 added that daughter Judith was to have preference in her choice of slaves (Madison County, Virginia Will Book 11: 5
2 CONC 25-527.).
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 September 1861 Waller Fishback renounced executorship of John Fishback's estate (Madison County, Virginia Will Book 11: 534.).
2 CONT
2 CONT 22 August 1861 Motion of Staunton Fishback, exor of John Fishback, to have Ann Fishback's dower in the land and slaves "lay off" and assign made (Madison County, Virginia Will Book 11: 593.).
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 November 1861 Invnetory and appraisal of John Fishback, total $13,450.44. Recorded 28 November 1861 (Madison County, Virginia Will Book 11: 537.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 	
