0 @N6000000002906170565@ NOTE 1738 BIRTH: Larry King, Rector Records,  (Hendersonville, Tennessee: 1986), 5, "3-3 DANIEL RECTOR, SR. s/o 2-1, B abt 1738 in VA.  M 7 Jan 1760 Nancy Ann Oldham.  C 4-8; 4-9; 4-10; 4-11;  4-12; 4-13; Abagail M John Battershell.  C
1 CONC ensus records for 1790 show Daniel Rector living in Allegheny CO., PA.  He D 1 May 1814."
1 CONT
1 CONT 1760 DEED: "(1) Fauquier Co. Deed Book 1, p.109.  Sept. 25, 1760, Thomas Lord Fairfax to Daniel Rector 
1 CONT 200 acres in the Manor of Leeds during the life of Daniel Rector, Ann his wife, and Henry Rector, Jr.  One would naturally expect the Henry Rector, Jr. mentioned in this lease to have been a son of Daniel and Ann Rector, probably 
1 CONC the eldest son, b. ca. 1758-59.  However, Henry is not specifically called son to Daniel in the lease, and it may be that the reference is to Daniel Rector's elder brother, Henry Rector, Jr."   B.C. Holtzclaw, John Jacob Rector of
1 CONC  Germanna and His Descendants, (Germanna Record No. 4), April 1963, Published by the Memorial Foundation of the Germanna Colonies in Virginia, Inc., www.germanna.org, p25.  
1 CONT
1 CONT 1768 DEED: "(2)  Fauquier Deed Book 3, p.226.  Aug 1, 1768, Lord Fairfax to Daniel Rector 175 acres  in the Manor of Leeds  during the life of Daniel Rector, Ann his wife and Conway Rector, his son." Germanna Record No. 4 at 25.  
1 CONC "As Daniel Rector was a lessee on Lord Fairfax's estate, he does not appear further in the records of Fairfax Co., [sic.[ in either the land tax lists nor the tithables list." Germanna Record No. 4 at 25.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1790 CENSUS: Allegheny County, Pennsylvania. "The U.S. Census of 1790 shows that in that year Daniel and Charles Rector were living in Allegheny Co., Pa., Daniel's family consisting of 1 male over 16, 2 males under 16, and 4 femal
1 CONC es; and Charles' family of 1 male over 16, 1 under 16, and 3 females. Further search in Pennsylvania or Indiana might give more information about Daniel Rector's family."  Germanna Record No. 4 at 26.
1 CONT
1 CONT According to Sharon Barnes <barnes@lclark.edu>, Daniel is mentioned in his son's (Charles) Revolutionary war record in Washington DC.
1 CONT
1 CONT Also published on World Family Tree Vol. 4, Ed. 1, Broderbund Software, Inc.,  Release date: August 23, 1996 Media: Family Archive CD Page: Tree #3074.  Also Brøderbund WFT Vol. 9, Ed. 1, Tree #2919.
1 CONT
1 CONT Daniel Rector Sr. married Nancy Oldham He born 8 Feb 1742 Va. Married to Nancy 7 Jan 1760. They had 7 children. He died 1 May 1814 in Clark Co. Ohio. She uses page 12 History of German Twp. Clark Co. Ohio She also refers to Rector
1 CONC  Family by Clifford Rector. 
