1 CONT "Here are my notes re Daniel and Nancy Ann Rector and their marriage: Identified as the daughter of Ann Augheny on pg 107 of Early Records - Hampshire Co., Virginia (Now West Virginia) compiled by Clara McSage and Laura Jones, pub
1 CONC lished 1969 by Genealogical Publishing Co., Baltimore, Maryland.  The record is of early wills and Nancy is identified as Ann's daughter, Nancy Rector.  The will was probated 8 April 1796.  Page 132 of the same book mentions "Laur
1 CONC ence Ross m. Susan Oldham, daughter of (John?) dead 1766 and AnnConway Oldham(?) who, a widow by 1766, married Darby Aughney."  From this entry it would appear that Nancy's father was "(John)?" who died 1766 and left the wife Ann 
1 CONC Conway Oldham who later married Darby Aughney.  Marriage to Daniel Rector 7 Jan 1760 was reported on pg 5 in the book Rector Records, authored and published (1986) by Larry King of Hendersonville Tennessee." Jan Oldham <joldham@in
1 CONC dy.net>
