0 @N6000000002906947097@ NOTE Hdanw@aol.com  View Contact Details  
1 CONT Date: Sat, 25 Sep 2004 22:26:48 EDT 
1 CONT To: GERMANNA_COLONIES-L@rootsweb.com 
1 CONT Subject: [GERMANNA] Button, Holtzclaw, Fishback  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Dear Deanna, you wrote:
1 CONT
1 CONT Robbie,
1 CONT
1 CONT I don't think my Button's went that way [Missouri?].   Harmon Button m 
1 CONT Sarah 
1 CONT Fishback f
1 CONT John Frederick Fishback m Ann Elizabeth  Holtzclaw.  Elizabeth's 
1 CONT parents
1 CONT wereWilliam Holtzclaw m Mrs Thomas  Holtzclaw (I don't know if this was 
1 CONT a
1 CONT sister-in-law or what?)  Hope this  will help you.
1 CONT
1 CONT Question to Deanna and other interested parties:
1 CONT
1 CONT I did a google.com search for Harmon Button (just curious to know 
1 CONT what's  
1 CONT *out there*) and came across a Harmon Button married to a Catherine 
1 CONT Kemper as  
1 CONT well as one married to Sarah Fishback as you state above.  As is usual 
1 CONT with  
1 CONT *stuff* on the net, there seems to be no documentation, nor even dates.
1 CONT
1 CONT Is this the same Harmon Button, or is this a different Harmon Button?
1 CONT
1 CONT According to one of John K. Gott's books (he compiled several of them)  
1 CONT called Fauquier County, Virginia Deeds, 1778-1785, this is a bill of 
1 CONT sale  [deed] 
1 CONT in Deed Book 7, Fauquier Co. (page 6 of Gott):  (This was  published by 
1 CONT Heritage Books, InC., Bowie, MD, 1993)
1 CONT
1 CONT Pages 68-70.  30 Sept 1778 B. & S. Bet. Nathaniel Williams &  
1 CONT Elizabeth.h.w. 
1 CONT [his wife] of Staff. Co. and Martin Pickett.. 100 pounds ..   part of 
1 CONT larger 
1 CONT tract div. bet. the sd. Nathaniel, Charles, Jessee and Pople  Williams 
1 CONT .. adj. 
1 CONT land of Pope Wms., Jesse Wms and Martin Pickett also the land  of John 
1 CONT Kamper, 
1 CONT Harmon Button, Frederick & Peter Kamper,  which was formerly the 
1 CONT property of 
1 CONT Jordan.. 195 a  Signed Nath'a.  Williams Wits:  William Pope, John 
1 CONT Mauzy, 
1 CONT Marget (X) Williams, Joseph  Blackwell.  Rec:  22 Feb. 1779 prov. by o. 
1 CONT [oath] of 
1 CONT Wm. Pople &  John Mauzy.  26 Apr. 1779 prov. by o. of Joseph Blackwell.
1 CONT
1 CONT Comment:  Fauquier Co. was formed 1759 from Prince William Co.,  while 
1 CONT it 
1 CONT seems Culpeper Co. was formed 1749 from Orange Co., VA.  
1 CONT
1 CONT E.W.Wallace
1 CONT a Kemper descendant
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Hdanw@aol.com  Add to Address Book 
1 CONT Date: Sun, 26 Sep 2004 00:36:57 EDT 
1 CONT To: GERMANNA_COLONIES-L@rootsweb.com 
1 CONT Subject: [GERMANNA] Button, Kemper, (Kamper) et al 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Thank you for sending the following message.  This seems to confirm  
1 CONT that a 
1 CONT Harmon Button prior to ca 1790 was married to a Catherine Kemper.
1 CONT
1 CONT >From Alcock's book:
1 CONT Button, Harmon, Deed book 5, p 499, 1774 John Smith  to him 1/3 of 1741 
1 CONT grant 
1 CONT to Henry, Mary, and Catherine Kemper; Smith "heir of  body" to 
1 CONT Catherine; 
1 CONT Button m. to her.  Will book 2, p 158, pr Minutes book  9, p. 237, Jan 
1 CONT 1790 by 
1 CONT Randolph Smith, Charles "Kamper".  Wife Catherine,  son Jacob, daus 
1 CONT Anne 
1 CONT Hockman, Sarah Sinsel, Susanna, Catherine, Rebekah, execs.  John 
1 CONT "Kamper" and Jacob 
1 CONT "Kamper" Jr.,  Minutes book 14, p 871, 1700, Jacob  Kemper surv exec of 
1 CONT Button 
1 CONT failing to act, admin de bonis granted to Elijah  Bashaw m. to an heir 
1 CONT (Catherine); sec. Ephraim and Jacob Kemper.
1 CONT
1 CONT Also  listed Harmon Button, Jr. and Jacob Button and Thomas Button
1 CONT
1 CONT My response:
1 CONT
1 CONT I found my notes about Henry Kemper (Kamper), which are rather cryptic, 
1 CONT and  
1 CONT which now require more study on my part:
1 CONT
1 CONT      HENRY KEMPER. (ca 1730-after Nov 1787)
1 CONT
1 CONT      Information for dates of Henry Kemper come from  NSDAR Gen Recs 
1 CONT Comm, 
1 CONT Lineage of Andrew Jackson Kemper.
1 CONT
1 CONT      Henry Kemper is probably earlier known as John  Henry Kemper, all 
1 CONT the 
1 CONT German children (males particularly) having the same first  name, with 
1 CONT the 
1 CONT second name being the "calling" name.  The name of John  Henry Kemper 
1 CONT appears in 
1 CONT early Northern Neck surveys and land grants.
1 CONT
1 CONT       Survey for Prince William Co., survey made  for Thomas Jordan, 11 
1 CONT Mar 
1 CONT 1739- 21 May 1740; between Carters Great Run &  Barrows Run on Rappa. 
1 CONT R. "adj 
1 CONT John Henry Kemper."
1 CONT
1 CONT       (Peggy Shomo Joyner's ABSTRACTS OF  VIRGINIA'S NORTHERN NECK 
1 CONT WARRANTS & 
1 CONT SURVEYS... DUNMORE, SHENANDOAH,  CULPEPER, PRINCE WILLIAM, FAUQUIER & 
1 CONT STAFFORD COUNTIES 1710-1780, V. III, p.  117.)
1 CONT
1 CONT At approximately the same time, John  Kemper/Kempar, apparently the 
1 CONT father, 
1 CONT had land surveyed.  "Wart adds  Peter Kemper, and the chain carrier was 
1 CONT Peter 
1 CONT Kemper.  However, at the  bottom:  N.d. - "in the name of Heni [Henry], 
1 CONT Catharina & Maria  Kemper."  These are probably all children of John 
1 CONT Kemper.
1 CONT
1 CONT Abstract of the actual grant, as opposed to  the survey, differs 
1 CONT somewhat in 
1 CONT wording:
1 CONT
1 CONT         Northern Neck Grant Bk E-408  Heni [Henry?], Catherine Kemper & 
1 CONT Maria 
1 CONT Kemper son and daughters of John  Kemper of Pr. William Co. 362 A in 
1 CONT said Co. 
1 CONT on the Great Run of Rappahannock R.  adj. Kemper's other land.  Thomas 
1 CONT Lee, 
1 CONT Esq., Heirs of Maj. Richard Buckner  decd.  Surv by Mr. John Savage.  
1 CONT 22 Jan 
1 CONT 1741. 
1 CONT
1 CONT       (Gertrude E. Gray, NORTHERN NECK LAND  GRANTS, Vol I)
1 CONT
1 CONT      One Henry Kemper with wife Lettis (Lettice) was in  Fauquier Co. 
1 CONT 1764 
1 CONT until at least 1784.
1 CONT
1 CONT      Fauquier Co. DB 2-23-24 gives information that  Henry Kemper and 
1 CONT Lettis 
1 CONT (Lettice) wife sold to Jeremiah Darnall 40 A on Licking  Run ... part 
1 CONT of a 
1 CONT tract taken up by John Fishback, John Huffman & Jacob  Holtzclaw by 
1 CONT Patent ... 21 
1 CONT Aug 1724 and conveyed from the above persons to John  Kemper father to 
1 CONT the 
1 CONT said Henry Kemper ... to Licking Run ... Mountjoy's line  ... (s) Henry 
1 CONT Kemper, 
1 CONT Lettis (X) Kemper.  Rec:  24 May 1764, ack. by  grantors.
1 CONT
1 CONT      A subsequent deed was made in 1784.  DB  8-191-194.  22 Nov 1784.  
1 CONT Bargain and sale.  Bet. Henry Kamper  and Lettice his wife and George 
1 CONT Green ... 125 
1 CONT pds. ... tract .. joining the land  taken up by Michael Mildren, now 
1 CONT Bernards 
1 CONT and the land taken up by John Dagg and  whereon the sd. Henry Kamper 
1 CONT now 
1 CONT lives .. cor. to land of sd. Bernard .. cor. to  Benjamin King .. by a 
1 CONT drain 
1 CONT making down the Piney Mountain .. side of Rogers  Branch .. white oak 
1 CONT marked I W. 
1 CONT H. W. cor. to Buckner .. 187 A .. (s) Henry  Kamper, Lettice (X) Kamper  
1 CONT Wits:  
1 CONT Joseph Blackwell, Joseph  Jackman  Rec:  22 Nov 1784. ack by grantors.
1 CONT
1 CONT   (John K. Gott, FAUQUIER COUNTY, VIRGINIA, DEEDS 1778-1785, Vol. 2  
1 CONT [Bowie, 
1 CONT MD:  Heritage Books, Inc., 1993], p. 81-82)
1 CONT
1 CONT Thanks for your interest.  Now I have to sort out whether these  
1 CONT pertain to 
1 CONT the same Henry Kamper and try to determine more about his  siblings.
1 CONT
1 CONT Back to the books (and film) when I get rid of some of my home chores 
1 CONT and  
1 CONT volunteer work!!!
1 CONT
1 CONT E.W.Wallace
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT >From Alcock's book:
1 CONT Button, Harmon, Deed book 5, p 499, 1774 John Smith  to him 1/3 of 1741 grant 
1 CONT to Henry, Mary, and Catherine Kemper; Smith "heir of  body" to Catherin
1 CONT Button m. to her.  Will book 2, p 158, pr Minutes book  9, p. 237, Jan 1790 by 
1 CONT Randolph Smith, Charles "Kamper".  Wife Catherine,  son Jacob, daus Anne 
1 CONT Hockman, Sarah Sinsel, Susanna, Catherine, Rebekah, execs.  John "Kamper" and Jacob 
1 CONT "Kamper" Jr.,  Minutes book 14, p 871, 1700, Jacob  Kemper surv exec of Button 
1 CONT failing to act, admin de bonis granted to Elijah  Bashaw m. to an heir 
1 CONT (Catherine); sec. Ephraim and Jacob Kemper.
0 @N6000000010202540307@ NOTE
1 CONT kemper
1 CONT 1. German: status name denoting a peasant farmer or serf, an agent noun derivative of Kamp 1.
1 CONT 2. Dutch: agent noun derivative of Kemp, i.e. an occupational name for someone who grew, processed, or used hemp.
1 CONT 3. German (possibly also Dutch): habitational name from any of the twelve places named Kempen in the Dutch-German border area.
0 @N6000000006348403983@ NOTE He was named after Rev. David Rice, D. D, friend and mentor of his father.
