1 CONT Deed Abstracts of Madison County, Virginia 1793 - 1804:  Madison County Deed Book 1 (1793-1796), Madison County Deed Book 2 (1796-1801) and Madison County Deed Book 3 (1801-1804), Abstracted and Published by Ruth and Sam Sparacio 
1 CONC (1986), p 13:
1 CONT Deed Book 1, p 109-110
1 CONT      On Margin.  "Examined & delivered John Fishback Exor of Michael Clore March 1819 -- 13 acres"
1 CONT      Indenture (no date) between Michael Delph and his wife, Marget, and Michael Clore .. for £ 8.15.6 .. sell land on Warters of the Robinson River near Dark Run .. 13 acres .. Adam Delph's line ..
1 CONT In presence of John Piner,                   Michael (X) Delph
1 CONT John Clore, Philip Snider                    Margt. (X) Delph
1 CONT      At a court held .. 26th June 1794 .. Indenture proved and ordered to be certified.
1 CONT      At a court held .. 24th July 1794 .. fully proved and ordered to be recorded.
1 CONT
1 CONT Madison County, Virginia 1840 Federal Census
1 CONT p 7
1 CONT      Jno. Fishback  1 male age 20-29
1 CONT                1 male age 60-69
1 CONT                1 female age 15-19
1 CONT                1 female age 30-39
1 CONT                1 female age 50-59
1 CONT                1 female age 80-89*
1 CONT *probably mother-in-law Margaret (Weaver) Clore (1752-1842)
1 CONT
1 CONT Madison County, Virginia 1860 Federal Census
1 CONT PO Oak Park, p 44-43, Dwelling 355, Family 355
1 CONT      John Fishback  81 M Va   Farmer $16,048/$12,530
1 CONT      Ann  "    77 F "
1 CONT      Judy "    56 F "
1 CONT      Staunton Fishback   40 M Va   Master Machinist --/$5146
1 CONT      Dicey E.  "    17 F "
1 CONT      George W. Jackwson 15 M "     App
1 CONT      Andrew J. Carpenter 14 M "    "[Cathi Frost bcfrost@comcast.net Fishback-Clore.GED]
